  "name": "CMV IgG AVIDITY",
  "code": "2712",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>&gt;40%- High Avidity<br>&lt;30% - Low Avidity<br>30-40% - Borderline</p>\n<p>Comment:<br>It is advisable to repeat the test in 2-3 weeks in order to evaluate a possible variation of percentage of Avidity.</p>\n<p><br>Avidity is low in the acute phase of infection and increases over a period of time. The presence of low avidity antibodies is therefore an&nbsp;indication of a recent or current infection.</p>\n<p><br>The result showing high avidity (particularly in transplanted patients) does not exclude the possibility that there has been a recent infection.&nbsp;In the case of new born babies, a low avidity is not an indication of a current acute infection. The test result should be used in conjunction with information available from the evaluation of the last history or other diagnostic procedures.</p>",
